This year, I had the opportunity to work on several large and high-visibility projects that aligned closely with my goals around data accuracy, automation, and end-to-end process improvement. Each project allowed me to contribute directly to the quality, reliability, and scalability of our team’s data operations. Below are my key accomplishments across the core initiatives I supported.

TITAN Project – End-to-End Data Migration Testing and Validation

One of my major accomplishments this year was my contribution to the TITAN migration project. Even though the actual migration work was handled by another team, I was responsible for validating the integrity and completeness of the data after it was moved from SQL Server to Snowflake.

I conducted detailed testing across multiple dimensions, including:

Verifying table structures, schema layouts, column names, and data types
Ensuring row counts and column counts matched between the source and target environments
Performing in-depth field-level comparisons to confirm that sensitive and high-value data behaved consistently in Snowflake.
Identifying mismatches in metadata and discrepancies between environments and tracing them back to the exact root cause
Collaborating with engineering and QA teams to ensure that corrections were implemented quickly and verified successfully

This work strengthened the reliability of the overall migration and gave leadership confidence that the new Snowflake environment could support downstream processes without data loss or degradation. It also improved my ability to build structured validation frameworks and approach testing with a high level of attention to detail.

EPMP Project – High-Volume API Automation and Scalable Workflow Design

Another major accomplishment this year was the development of a fully automated and scalable workflow for the EPMP Preferences API. The goal was to process over 1.1 million MBI records within strict time constraints while ensuring complete accuracy and traceability.

Key accomplishments in this project include:

Designing and coding an asynchronous Python workflow capable of parallelizing API calls to handle extremely high volumes
Implementing chunking logic, retry strategies, error categorization, and token refresh mechanisms
Building detailed logs for business users, QA teams, and future audits/
Creating supporting documentation covering workflow logic, error handling, output file structures, and production monitoring steps
Partnering with the business to define scheduling requirements and implementing the workflow to run three times per week through Alteryx Server
Ensuring all 1.1M records were accounted for by validating counts across raw input files, output files, and error logs

This project significantly improved the speed, quality, and consistency of the EPMP preference intake process. It also deepened my skills in large-scale API integration, asynchronous design patterns, and enterprise-level automation.

Text/SMS Campaign – Automated SMS Manager Integration and Workflow Development

In the Text/SMS campaign initiative, I collaborated closely with business partners to automate the entire phone handling and outbound messaging workflow using the SMS Manager API. This work required both technical implementation and cross-functional alignment.

My accomplishments include:

Designing and building the complete phone lifecycle automation: phone creation, phone lookup, program subscription, and sending SMS messages
Developing logic to dynamically manage access tokens that expire every 30 minutes
Creating reusable Python functions that standardize phone formats, attach metadata (GMPI_ID), and handle error cases
Generating output logs that track phone creation, subscription results, and message delivery details
Building two Alteryx workflows:

Workflow 1: Load phone records into the SMS Opt-In Raw table
Workflow 2: Match, validate, and load cleaned records from Raw into the final SMS Opt-In table
Ensuring data quality by standardizing inconsistent phone numbers and resolving mismatches with existing system records
Taking responsibility for delivering monthly short-code SMS sends from September to December

This workstream improved the accuracy of SMS outreach, standardized how phone data flows into the platform.

New-to-Therapy (NTT) Automation – Weekly Refresh, Validation, and Table Enhancements

I also contributed significantly to improving the New-to-Therapy (NTT) process. This work required both technical cleanup and logic improvement to support higher-quality reporting.

Major accomplishments include:

Automating the weekly refresh of the NTT table
Validating incoming loads to ensure the data met business expectations
Identifying and resolving mismatches between weekly data snapshots
Designing and testing a new TEMP_NTT version of the table with:

Primary key columns
Audit columns (inserted date, updated date, updated by, etc.)
Building logic to copy data from NTT into the enhanced TEMP_NTT table for validation and downstream use
Running comparison scripts to ensure both tables were aligned and identifying discrepancies early
Making the workflow easier to monitor and safer to refresh during weekly runs

This work strengthened the reliability of the NTT dataset and improved the team’s ability to track changes over time with better transparency and accuracy.

